        <p class="text-xl text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-8">
          You've dug through the couch cushions, patted down every jacket and walked the parking lot twice. Nothing. The key was the only one you had, and it's gone. So here's how to replace lost car keys. Show that the car is yours, hand the VIN to a locksmith or a dealer, get a new key cut and programmed, and then have the lost one wiped from the car's memory. A mobile locksmith can do the whole thing right next to your car, and often in a single visit.
        </p>

        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Below, we go through each step, what to dig up before you call, and how to pick between a locksmith and a dealership.
        </p>

        <blockquote class="border-l-4 border-[#A61E22] bg-[#F8F8F5] px-6 py-4 my-8 not-italic">
          <p class="font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-2">Key Takeaways</p>
