            <li>No spare and no original? You can still get a new key. The VIN and proof you own the car carry most of the load.</li>
            <li>Newer keys hold a chip the car has to recognize. Cutting the metal is the easy half. Programming needs special equipment.</li>
            <li>Once the new key works, get the lost one erased from the car's memory.</li>
            <li>A mobile locksmith comes to the car, so most of the time you skip the tow.</li>
          </ul>
        </blockquote>

