              <span class="text-[#A61E22] text-2xl group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform">+</span>
            </summary>
            <p class="mt-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Usually not. A mobile locksmith carries the cutting and programming tools to the car, so there's no tow.</p>
          </details>

                  <details class="bg-[#F8F8F5] rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-200 group">
            <summary class="font-bold text-[#1A1F22] text-lg cursor-pointer flex justify-between items-center">
              Can a locksmith make a key without the VIN?
              <span class="text-[#A61E22] text-2xl group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform">+</span>
            </summary>
            <p class="mt-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">The VIN is the fastest route, and it's printed on your registration and insurance card. Some vehicles can still be keyed from the lock itself. Have the VIN handy anyway.</p>
          </details>

                  <details class="bg-[#F8F8F5] rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-200 group">
            <summary class="font-bold text-[#1A1F22] text-lg cursor-pointer flex justify-between items-center">
              Will my old key still start the car after a new one is programmed?
              <span class="text-[#A61E22] text-2xl group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform">+</span>
            </summary>
            <p class="mt-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">On many vehicles the lost key can be erased from the car's memory, which stops it from working. Ask the technician to do that, especially if the key might have been stolen.</p>
          </details>

                  <details class="bg-[#F8F8F5] rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-200 group">
            <summary class="font-bold text-[#1A1F22] text-lg cursor-pointer flex justify-between items-center">
              Is it better to use a locksmith or the dealership?
              <span class="text-[#A61E22] text-2xl group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform">+</span>
            </summary>
            <p class="mt-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">For most makes, a mobile locksmith is quicker and comes to you. Some specialty or very new models may need the dealer. A good locksmith will say which camp yours falls in.</p>
          </details>

                  <details class="bg-[#F8F8F5] rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-200 group">
            <summary class="font-bold text-[#1A1F22] text-lg cursor-pointer flex justify-between items-center">
              What if my key fob battery is just dead?
              <span class="text-[#A61E22] text-2xl group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform">+</span>
            </summary>
            <p class="mt-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Swap in a fresh battery and try the hidden mechanical key inside the fob. Still no luck? The fob needs reprogramming.</p>
          </details>

                </div>
      </div>
    </div>
